    "extracted text": "The paper studies two Al-Mg-Mn alloys with and without Sc and Zr additions. The alloys underwent various homogenization treatments (300°C, 350°C, and 440°C for 8h) followed by hot rolling, cold rolling, and then annealing at different temperatures (270°C, 300°C, and 330°C for 1h). For Al-Mg-Mn alloy, the optimized homogenization process for removing micro-segregation is 440°C×8h. For Al-Mg-Mn-Sc-Zr alloy, the optimized homogenization process for maximum precipitation strengthening of secondary Al3(Sc, Zr) particles is 300°C×8h.",
